WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.020
- So the question is, does section three

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.870
of the 14th Amendment
apply to President Trump,

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.850
in the sense that it bars people

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.580
who have committed sedition
from holding office

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.650
in the United States?

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.240
Putting aside the question
of whether President Trump

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.850
actually committed sedition or not,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.920
the 14th Amendment, this particular clause

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.060
was enabled to prevent members

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.010
of the Confederacy from holding office

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.410
in the federal government again.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.370
And for better or worse,

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.580
this section of the 14th Amendment

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.100
has almost never been used

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.710
because almost as soon
as Congress passed it,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.060
they granted a waiver to almost everyone

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.320
that served for the
South in the Civil War.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.760
And there are tons of open questions

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.500
in terms of whether
this is self-executing,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.270
whether you actually have to hold a trial.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.370
And we just don't know the answer

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.600
to these questions right now.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.950
So it's a completely open
question if it applies

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.370
to President Trump and
to what extent it does.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.120
So stay tuned for&amp; more election coverage

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.553
and I'll see you in court.

